```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Set `resizableColumns={true}` to enable column resizing
- ✅ Users can drag column borders to resize
- ✅ Column widths are automatically synced between header and body
- ✅ Resizing works with virtual scrolling
- ✅ Column width sync happens automatically when scrolling stops (150ms delay)
- ✅ Column widths are preserved during virtual scrolling

**⚠️ CRITICAL: Container Layout Requirements for Column Alignment**

**When using `EndlessScrollDataGrid` with content above it (charts, stats, etc.), ensure proper container structure:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Simple container structure
<Box
    ref={tableContainerRef}
    sx={{
        position: "relative",
        isolation: "isolate",
    }}
>
    <EndlessScrollDataGrid
        // ... props
    />
</Box>
```

**If you have content above the grid (charts, stats sections), ensure the content container has layout constraints:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Charts/stats container with layout constraints
<Box sx={{ mb: 3, mt: 3 }}>
    <Box
        sx={{
            display: "grid",
            gridTemplateColumns: {
                xs: "1fr",
                md: "1fr 1fr",
                lg: "1fr 1fr 1fr",
            },
            gap: { xs: 2, sm: 3 },
            mb: 3,
            width: "100%",           // ✅ Prevent width fluctuations
            boxSizing: "border-box", // ✅ Include padding/borders in width
            contain: "layout",        // ✅ Isolate layout calculations
        }}
    >
        {/* Charts/stats content */}
    </Box>
</Box>

{/* Virtual Grid */}
<Box
    ref={tableContainerRef}
    sx={{
        position: "relative",
        isolation: "isolate",
    }}
>
    <EndlessScrollDataGrid
        // ... props
    />
</Box>
```

**Common Issues and Solutions:**

- ❌ **Problem**: Column alignment breaks when scrolling up
  - **Cause**: Content above grid (charts/stats) causing layout shifts
  - **Solution**: Add `width: "100%"`, `boxSizing: "border-box"`, and `contain: "layout"` to content container

- ❌ **Problem**: Columns resize unexpectedly during scroll
  - **Cause**: Container width recalculations from responsive grid layouts
  - **Solution**: Use `contain: "layout"` to isolate layout calculations

- ❌ **Problem**: Header and body columns misaligned
  - **Cause**: Parent container width changes affecting grid container
  - **Solution**: Ensure grid container has stable width (`position: "relative"`, `isolation: "isolate"`)

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Keep grid container Box simple - only `position: "relative"` and `isolation: "isolate"`
- ✅ Add layout constraints to content containers above the grid
- ✅ Use `contain: "layout"` on responsive grid containers to prevent layout shifts
- ✅ Never add toolbar override styles or width constraints to the grid container Box
- ✅ Column width sync is automatic - don't manually trigger sync during scroll

